---
/**
 * Contact page illustration: a line-drawn tree with two hanging baya nests,
 * three leaf clouds and three of the logo birds.
 *
 * Motion (src/scripts/contact-tree.ts), all off for reduced motion:
 * - When the tree scrolls into view the birds greet the visitor: the nest bird
 *   peeks, then the two perched birds flutter, using the logo's flutter.
 * - For the next 30 seconds, every 3 to 6 seconds one bird makes a small move
 *   (flutter, tail flick, glance the other way; the nest bird ducks and peeks).
 *   This stops as soon as someone starts filling in the form.
 * - A fluttering bird's branch dips and springs back, carrying its cloud and nest.
 * - Hovering a bird (mouse or trackpad) wakes it, and all three celebrate when
 *   the contact form is sent.
 *
 * Lines are 2px outlines and 1.25px details at every size (non-scaling strokes).
 * Shapes whose outlines join (the wood, each cloud) are drawn twice: a 4px
 * outline pass, then a fill pass that hides the inner half and the overlaps.
 * The artwork is generated; edit coordinates with care.
 */
---

